    "title": "Fire crews battle grass fires south of Abilene Regional Airport - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shelly Womack No media credit provided. ,\n5 hours ago\nABILENE, Texas ( KTAB/KRBC ) — Firefighters are battling three grass fires south of the Abilene Regional Airport Wednesday afternoon.\nThe fires broke out on August 5, sending a large plume of smoke into the air that could be seen from across Abilene.\nDetails about what sparked the fire have not yet been released. It is also unclear whether the fire has been brought under control.\nThe Potosi, Eula and Abilene Fire Departments are currently on scene. One fire chief believes the fires may have been caused by something dragging from a vehicle, though that has not been confirmed.\nDrivers are urged to avoid the area and use caution while emergency crews work at the scene.\nBigCountryHomepage will update this story as more information becomes available.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KTAB - BigCountryHomepage.com.",
